### =====================================================
### Indexer Field Sample Requests
### Demonstrates how an indexer writes source documents: fields the
### target index doesn't define (source properties and metadata_*
### values) are left out instead of failing the batch, and Edm.Int64
### values are indexed exactly.
### =====================================================
###
### SETUP ORDER:
### 1. Create the index, the data source and the indexer
### 2. Run the indexer and check its status
### 3. Search the indexed documents
### 4. Cleanup
###
### Prerequisites:
### - The simulator running at https://localhost:7250
### - REST Client extension for VS Code
### - @sampleDataPath set to this repo's samples/sample-data folder
###   (the source files are in samples/sample-data/indexer-fields/)
###
### Simulator only: Azure has no filesystem data source, so unlike the
### other feature samples this file has no [AZURE] requests.
### =====================================================

@baseUrl = {{$dotenv BASE_URL}}
@apiVersion = {{$dotenv API_VERSION}}
@adminKey = {{$dotenv ADMIN_KEY}}
@queryKey = {{$dotenv QUERY_KEY}}
@sampleDataPath = C:/Projets/AzureAISimulator/samples/sample-data

# =====================================================
# 1. CREATE THE INDEX, THE DATA SOURCE AND THE INDEXER
# =====================================================

### Create an index that defines only some of the source's properties
PUT {{baseUrl}}/indexes/indexer-field-sample?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "name": "indexer-field-sample",
  "fields": [
    { "name": "id", "type": "Edm.String", "key": true, "filterable": true },
    { "name": "name", "type": "Edm.String", "searchable": true },
    { "name": "views", "type": "Edm.Int64", "filterable": true, "sortable": true }
  ]
}

### Create a data source over the JSON files in indexer-fields/
PUT {{baseUrl}}/datasources/indexer-field-files?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "name": "indexer-field-files",
  "type": "filesystem",
  "credentials": { "connectionString": "{{sampleDataPath}}" },
  "container": { "name": "indexer-fields" }
}

### Create an indexer that parses each file as one JSON document
PUT {{baseUrl}}/indexers/indexer-field-indexer?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{adminKey}}

{
  "name": "indexer-field-indexer",
  "dataSourceName": "indexer-field-files",
  "targetIndexName": "indexer-field-sample",
  "parameters": { "configuration": { "parsingMode": "json" } }
}

# =====================================================
# 2. RUN THE INDEXER
# =====================================================

### Run the indexer
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexers/indexer-field-indexer/run?api-version={{apiVersion}}
api-key: {{adminKey}}

### Check its status: both documents succeed, though the files have properties the index doesn't define
GET {{baseUrl}}/indexers/indexer-field-indexer/status?api-version={{apiVersion}}
api-key: {{adminKey}}

# =====================================================
# 3. SEARCH THE INDEXED DOCUMENTS
# =====================================================

### Both documents are indexed, with only the fields the index defines → p1, p2
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/indexer-field-sample/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "orderby": "id"
}

### Int64 values are exact: 9007199254740993 isn't rounded to the nearest double → p1
POST {{baseUrl}}/indexes/indexer-field-sample/docs/search?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
api-key: {{queryKey}}

{
  "search": "*",
  "filter": "views eq 9007199254740993"
}

# =====================================================
# 4. CLEANUP
# =====================================================

### Delete the indexer
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/indexers/indexer-field-indexer?api-version={{apiVersion}}
api-key: {{adminKey}}

### Delete the data source
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/datasources/indexer-field-files?api-version={{apiVersion}}
api-key: {{adminKey}}

### Delete the index
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/indexes/indexer-field-sample?api-version={{apiVersion}}
api-key: {{adminKey}}
